{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"vapoury-attack-lamb","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# A failed tickets-branch push is UNDELIVERABLE (not merely uninformative) on the async, library and MCP write paths\n\nSplit out of [rebar:2a76-c9d9-4e8a-471b] as RC-3 of its proven root-cause account. 2a76 fixes the\nCLI/synchronous path (the rejection reason and the unpushed-commit backlog now reach the\nwarning). This ticket covers the surfaces where the warning is not merely content-free but is\nnever delivered at all, so 2a76's fix is a no-op for them.\n\n## Proven, measured (rebar-debug Phase 1; real `pre-receive` decline against a local bare origin)\n\n1. **`sync.push = async`** -- a first-class documented policy value (`docs/concurrency.md:302-310`).\n   `src/rebar/_store/push.py:128-141` re-spawns the push as a detached\n   `subprocess.Popen(..., stdout=DEVNULL, stderr=DEVNULL, start_new_session=True)`, never waited.\n   Every warning the child emits, including the terminal one at `push.py:296`, is discarded by\n   the OS. Only an `OSError` at SPAWN time is logged (`push.py:144-148`).\n   MEASURED: `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=async rebar comment <id> x` against a rejecting hook ->\n   exit 0, stderr COMPLETELY EMPTY, `origin/tickets..HEAD` still incremented.\n   The inconsistency is internal to one function: the authors already closed this hazard for\n   the spawn case at `push.py:144-148` and left the far likelier push-failure case DEVNULL'd.\n\n2. **Library embedders** -- `src/rebar/__init__.py:131` attaches a `NullHandler` to the `rebar`\n   root; `install_stderr_handler` is called only from `_cli/__init__.py:418` and\n   `mcp_server.py:690`. MEASURED: in-process `rebar.comment(...)` -> returned normally, stderr\n   EMPTY, no push status in the return value.\n\n3. **MCP** -- the handler IS installed (`mcp_server.py:688,690`) but targets the SERVER's stderr;\n   the writing agent reads only the tool result, and `_mcp_writes.py` declares no push field.\n   (Static evidence; this limb was not driven end-to-end and should be confirmed first.)\n\n4. **Reconciler subprocess** -- `_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py:488,490` installs the handler\n   on the `rebar_reconciler` root only, while `rebar._store.push` resolves under `rebar`. So\n   reconciler-initiated pushes are mute even in the foreground.\n\n## Contract constraint (load-bearing)\n\n`docs/concurrency.md:296-299` makes \"never fails the caller\" AUTHORITATIVE INTENT, pinned by\n`push.py:9-11` (\"ALWAYS returns None\") and `tests/unit/test_store.py:151,156` (`# no raise`).\nThe remedy must be a SIGNAL -- an un-DEVNULL'd child, a persisted pending-state, an MCP result\nfield -- and must NEVER become an exception or a non-zero exit.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] the async path's push failure is observable (e.g. child stderr routed to a log file or the\n      failure persisted as state a later command reports) rather than discarded to /dev/null\n- [ ] the MCP limb is first CONFIRMED end-to-end (drive a rejecting origin through the MCP\n      `comment` tool and inspect the JSON result), then either given a push-status field or an\n      explicit recorded decision that it should not have one\n- [ ] a test drives a REAL rejected push on each covered surface and asserts the caller sees it\n- [ ] the best-effort contract is preserved: no write is failed and no exit code changes\n","id":"e1ed-b700-c442-4d0c","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"A failed tickets-branch push is undeliverable on the async, library and MCP write paths"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786079420691433001,"uuid":"273514ca-a71b-46d1-bb47-3aaa505d024c"}